1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,440
I'm scared. Scared to dig too deep into myself.

2
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:34,920
Hmm. Your work's not bad. It's alright, but... How do I put this? Readers want to see what

3
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:39,760
makes an artist tick. You gotta dig deep down into yourself. That's what art's all about.

4
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:46,760
You say you're 29 now? Yeah, our magazine might not be the best fit for you.

5
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:50,760
The 2006 World Cup in Germany is only 26 days away.

6
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:55,760
If only I'd done things different is a phrase that pops into my head every day.

7
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,760
I don't think about it too seriously though.

8
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:01,760
Just words. As soon as they come to mind.

9
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:04,760
They disappear.

10
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:08,760
I'm scared. Scared to dig too deep into myself.

11
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:19,760
Heading out on a delivery.

12
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:21,760
Okay. Drive safe.

13
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:24,760
I'm heading out on one too.

14
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:27,760
Kay, drive safe out there.

15
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:31,760
Poojinuma, keep your stomach away from that pizza, you hear?

16
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,760
Geez. Is that what kids are calling humor these days?

17
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:36,760
I will.

18
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:47,760
Fun fact. She says that to me every day. It's the only thing she says to me.

19
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:54,760
Far as I can tell, she's got zero feelings for me. She's so weird. Too weird, too young.

20
00:01:54,760 --> 00:02:12,760
There it was. It happened again. Where is it? Something's not right. But what?

21
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:25,760
Hey! You in the truck! Pull over!

22
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:27,760
Yo! Stop the truck!

23
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:28,760
Wait!

24
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:42,760
Wait, that's Poojinuma. What's he doing?

25
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:46,760
Goddammit! I can't believe I'm doing this!

26
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:49,760
Why am I doing this?

27
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,760
Why am I doing this?

28
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:56,760
Come on!

29
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,760
Oh my god!

30
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:05,760
You okay?

31
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:18,760
What am I looking at?

32
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:23,760
Oh. It's my life flashing before my eyes.

33
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:28,760
This is what happens when you get involved with other people's problems.

34
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:37,760
Oh well. If I'm dead, I'm dead. Who cares?

35
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:41,760
Huh?

36
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:43,760
You opened your eyes.

37
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:48,760
It's about time. You were out for two days.

38
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:55,760
Katagiri?

39
00:03:55,760 --> 00:04:00,760
Hiya, Sleeping Beauty. So, do you know who you are and how you got here?

40
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:06,760
Satoru Fujinuma. I'm 29. I was chasing the truck and I got hit.

41
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:11,760
Awesome! The truck said it's a miracle you didn't get hurt more.

42
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:16,760
Do you want me to go call someone for you? Like a friend or girlfriend or something?

43
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:21,760
Uh-uh. There isn't anyone I want to bother telling.

44
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:24,760
Snip, snip.

45
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:27,760
I don't get it. That's supposed to be funny?

46
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:30,760
No, I'm just trying to cut through that thick cocoon you're in.

47
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:33,760
You come off like the type who doesn't open up or care about anyone.

48
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:38,760
The non-laughing type. But after the other day, I know better.

49
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:39,760
How so?

50
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:43,760
You saved that kid's life. I was right there and I saw the whole thing go down.

51
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:48,760
And you know that truck driver? Well, I heard he had a heart attack and died at the wheel.

52
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:50,760
I still don't get how you noticed that.

53
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:51,760
Lucky, I guess.

54
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:56,760
Yeah, well, the truck crashed into a warehouse and amazingly, you and the driver were the only casualties.

55
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:58,760
What about the damages?

56
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:02,760
I told our manager what happened and he says insurance will take care of the bike in the other car.

57
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,760
And then when you get better, come back to work.

58
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,760
That's good news.

59
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:09,760
Ha! I caught you smiling.

60
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:15,760
How come you work at the pizza place? It can't be for the money.

61
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:17,760
Wow. Now there's a personal question.

62
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:19,760
Oh, sorry, was it?

63
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:26,760
Mm-hmm. In fact, you're the first person to ever ask me that. I work there because I have a dream.

64
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:27,760
That's cool.

65
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,760
Don't you want to know what it is?

66
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:37,760
Well, aren't you worried that it jinxed it for you? Besides, if it didn't come true, people would think you're a loser.

67
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:45,760
Oh, I'm not worried about telling anyone. The more I talk about it, the better the chance it'll come true. That's what I think anyway.

68
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:50,760
Wait. Where have I heard that before?

69
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,760
You know what? I decided I'm not going to tell you about it after all.

70
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:55,760
What?

71
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:57,760
It's not like we're dating or anything like that.

72
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:02,760
I'm gonna let the nurse know you're awake and then I'm going home. See ya!

73
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:07,760
Man, she's weird.

74
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:11,760
I have a name for what happens to me.

75
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:13,760
Revival.

76
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:17,760
It never benefits me, but I play along with it anyway.

77
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:24,760
When it happens, I go back in time anywhere from one to five minutes.

78
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:28,760
And it always happens before something bad goes down.

79
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:35,760
It's like someone's forcing me to fix whatever's gone wrong, so I start looking for the one thing that seems, you know, off.

80
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:39,760
I've managed to stop a lot of tragedies, so far.

81
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:44,760
Most of the time, I fix whatever bad's supposed to happen and everything comes out okay.

82
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:49,760
But sometimes, like this time, things go bad for me.

83
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:50,760
For me.

84
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,760
Oh. Hey there, Satoru.

85
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:09,760
Hey, Mom.

86
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:15,760
I went to the hospital, but you were out cold. Sorry I didn't stay, but I got bored watching you sleep.

87
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:18,760
So, how's your head doing, kiddo?

88
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:20,760
It's fine.

89
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:24,760
Yeah, right. They told me you had a head-on with a car.

90
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:27,760
I'll be staying for a while.

91
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:30,760
Huh? What do you mean, you're staying?

92
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:35,760
What do you think I mean? I want to make sure my little guy's okay. A car hit you, for Christ's sakes.

93
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:39,760
You don't have to. I said I'm fine. Anyway, I only have one futon.

94
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:43,760
No worries. I can make do with the sleeping bag I found in the closet.

95
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:45,760
A hotel's better.

96
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:47,760
Nah, hotel's too expensive.

97
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:50,760
Oh, then I can pay you back for the hospital and...

98
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:52,760
So keep it and we'll call it my rent.

99
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:58,760
She's 52, but looks the same as when I was a kid. Same attitude, too.

100
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:02,760
Satoru, do I have to change trains to get to Ueno?

101
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:04,760
No, you don't.

102
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:05,760
Wait, you want to go sightseeing?

103
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:11,760
Well, I did come all the way from Hokkaido. Besides, if I had to look at your face all day, I'd get bored.

104
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,760
You haven't even been here a whole day yet, Mom.

105
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:16,760
Come on. Let's eat.

106
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:26,760
I took over your futon and TV. Sorry.

107
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:31,760
No, it's cool. This sucks. If I need to use the bathroom later, I'll have to tiptoe around her.

108
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:37,760
Hey, if you need to use the bathroom later, don't worry about tiptoeing around me. I'm gonna sleep like a log tonight.

109
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:39,760
Witch.

110
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:46,760
And now for our next story. Yesterday evening, we told you about a first grade girl from Saitama who went missing.

111
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:51,760
Well, I'm happy to report that this morning, she was found walking along a road in Yokohama.

112
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:55,760
Hey, kiddo. You remember back then?

113
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:56,760
Back when?

114
00:08:56,760 --> 00:09:00,760
You were in fifth grade and something like this happened in the neighborhood.

115
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:02,760
Do you remember that?

116
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:11,760
It's okay if you don't. Us parents got together and decided the best thing was to try to get you kids to forget about it.

117
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,760
You didn't know, but your life was in danger.

118
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:25,760
When I was in fifth grade, a kidnapping?

119
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:39,760
I remember. Two classmates of mine went missing.

120
00:09:54,760 --> 00:10:00,760
I was a shy kid. And then I met this local guy, Yuki. He'd play with me.

121
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:06,760
Yuki wasn't his real name, but I called him that. He'd always say, have courage.

122
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:11,760
I bet I know what the most popular kid in your class is like.

123
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:13,760
Huh?

124
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:18,760
For starters, I bet he's cheerful and good at sports. He ain't afraid to speak up for himself.

125
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,760
And he can be a goofball too, but not when it comes to something he's super into.

126
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:24,760
Whoa.

127
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,760
No biggie. Popular folks are always like that.

128
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,760
Y-you could be like that too if you want to.

129
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:33,760
Just follow that kid's lead. And don't be shy.

130
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,760
Cause if you have courage, you can do anything.

131
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:45,760
Six months after my classmates disappeared, Jun Shiratori was arrested for kidnapping and murder.

132
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:48,760
It was Yuki.

133
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:54,760
Why'd you have to buy so much?

134
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:56,760
You got those okay?

135
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:59,760
I'm gonna make enough curry to last you a whole week.

136
00:11:04,760 --> 00:11:06,760
Oh, honey. See, that's why I told you not to run.

137
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:09,760
I told you not to run. Let's go and get you another one.

138
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,760
Hey, you okay back there?

139
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:22,760
Yeah.

140
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:24,760
You got those okay?

141
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:27,760
I'm gonna make enough curry to last you a whole week.

142
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:28,760
Another revival.

143
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:37,760
Oh, honey. See, that's why I told you not to run. Let's go and get you another one.

144
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:42,760
Crap. Where is it? Come on, man. Find it. Find it.

145
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:43,760
Find it. Find it.

146
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:46,760
Hey, Mom. You notice anything weird?

147
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:48,760
Like what?

148
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:50,760
Look around. Don't you feel like something's off here?

149
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,760
I don't know what you're talking about.

150
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:58,760
Wait. Come to think of it, you said the same thing when you were a little kid, too.

151
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:00,760
Did I?

152
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:02,760
Yeah. Remember the fire?

153
00:12:03,760 --> 00:12:04,760
Oh!

154
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:09,760
Was that guy looking at me?

155
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:23,760
Nothing happened.

156
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:29,760
Hey, Fujinuma!

157
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:31,760
Over here!

158
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:37,760
She's your mom? She looked so young, I thought she was your sister.

159
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:39,760
Do you believe in witches?

160
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:40,760
I do now.

161
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:42,760
Is she mad at you or something?

162
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:44,760
No.

163
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:46,760
Um...Irie?

164
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:48,760
Would you like to come over and have some curry with us?

165
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:50,760
Yes, ma'am! I totally would!

166
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:52,760
Thank you for the invite! I'll even help you make it!

167
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:54,760
Seriously?

168
00:12:54,760 --> 00:13:05,760
No way! You draw manga?

169
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:07,760
Does that shock you?

170
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:10,760
Not at all. If it's on Wicketanica, it must be true.

171
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:12,760
You looked me up?

172
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:14,760
Of course. Why not?

173
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,760
Okay, guys. Dig in.

174
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:19,760
Why?

175
00:13:19,760 --> 00:13:20,760
Cause I don't want you to.

176
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:22,760
This smells yummy!

177
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:24,760
Wow! It is yummy!

178
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:29,760
You did help. You know, for someone so young, you really know your way around a curry.

179
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:31,760
So how long have you guys been dating?

180
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:33,760
Oh no, it's not like that.

181
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:36,760
He's more like a friend.

182
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,760
A friend I have tons of respect for.

183
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:42,760
What? Too spicy for you?

184
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:44,760
No. It's great.

185
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:48,760
It was super nice meeting you.

186
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:52,760
I can give you a lift to the station.

187
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:55,760
It's already so late. You can spend the night if you want.

188
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:58,760
No, she can't, Mom. She's in high school.

189
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:02,760
Thanks for having me over. And for the ride, Satoru.

190
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:06,760
No worries. Just keep an eye out for cops, okay?

191
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:07,760
Mm-hmm.

192
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:15,760
Welcome home.

193
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:18,760
Let's get something straight, Mom.

194
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:21,760
She's not a potential wife for me. She's my co-worker.

195
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:24,760
Oh, please. Don't be so dense.

196
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:26,760
You hurt her. She respects you.

197
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:28,760
You totally have a shot with her.

198
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:30,760
God, she was just being polite.

199
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:32,760
Don't go blowing a compliment out of proportion.

200
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:36,760
I'm not. She doesn't seem like the type who'd say that unless you meant it.

201
00:14:37,760 --> 00:14:38,760
Huh?

202
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,760
Oh, by the way, your landlady came over asking about the rent.

203
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:43,760
Great.

204
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:45,760
Satoru, about this afternoon.

205
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,760
What?

206
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:48,760
In the market's parking lot.

207
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:50,760
Yeah? What's up? What about it?

208
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,760
I think you might have stopped a kid from getting snatched.

209
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,760
You're kidding!

210
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:57,760
You're right. I am kidding.

211
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:03,760
I remember.

212
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:18,760
She was a classmate of mine 18 years ago. She was one of the kidnapper's victims.

213
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:20,760
Kayo Hinazuki.

214
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:25,760
We weren't friends or anything, but I'd always see her alone at the park.

215
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:35,760
That night at the park was the last time I saw Kayo.

216
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:39,760
No, you don't get it! I could have saved her!

217
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:43,760
If I'd have asked her to walk home with me, she'd still be alive!

218
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:48,760
Back then, all I wanted was to forget how guilty I felt.

219
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:53,760
I know my mom did everything she could to erase it from my memory.

220
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:56,760
Readers want to see what makes an artist tick.

221
00:15:57,760 --> 00:16:00,760
You gotta dig deep down into yourself. That's what art's all about.

222
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:07,760
His car had rental plates. He was gonna kidnap her for sure.

223
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:11,760
Did he change his mind cause I saw him?

224
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:14,760
He turned away like he was hiding his face.

225
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:17,760
He definitely knew me.

226
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,760
And I know I've seen those eyes somewhere.

227
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:22,760
But on who?

228
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:24,760
And where?

229
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:25,760
When?

230
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:32,760
That's it!

231
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:34,760
I remember now.

232
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:36,760
Oh my god.

233
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:38,760
Shiratori's not the killer after all.

234
00:16:38,760 --> 00:16:48,760
Hey, it's Sachiko.

235
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:50,760
Yeah, it's been a while.

236
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:56,760
The statute of limitations on those murders ran out a while ago.

237
00:16:56,760 --> 00:17:03,760
And god knows how many kids he must have killed over the past 18 years.

238
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:08,760
The case is anything but closed.

239
00:17:09,760 --> 00:17:11,760
I have to talk to Satoru.

240
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:15,760
The time's come to set him straight on what happened back then.

241
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:20,760
Satoru?

242
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:21,760
Satoru?

243
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:39,760
I was right.

244
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:41,760
Have to call Satoru.

245
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:44,760
Tell him to stay away.

246
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:46,760
Tell him sorry.

247
